 on the same subnet. University and hotel Wi-Fi often block broadcast or isolate
 clients from each other; a phone hotspot or a lab switch works. The macOS firewall
 must allow incoming connections for `java`. TCP still works with `--host <ip>`.
+
+## 11. Chat rooms (new in M6, extension C)
+
+**Model.** Every registered client is in exactly **one** room at a time. Everybody
+starts in the room **`lobby`**. A room exists while at least one client is in it;
+there is no command to create or delete rooms.
+
+**Room names** follow the nickname rules (1–20 letters/digits of any alphabet, `_`,
+`-`). A leading `#` is ignored and names are case-insensitive: `#Games` = `games`.
+The server always writes them in lower case, without `#`.
+
+**New requests**
+
+| type | fields | meaning | reply |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `JOIN` | `room`: string | leave the current room and enter `room` | `OK`, or `ERROR 400` (bad name) |
+| `LEAVE` | — | go back to `lobby` | `OK` |
+
+`JOIN` to the room you are already in, and `LEAVE` while in the lobby, are accepted
+(`OK`) and change nothing.
+
+**Changed behaviour**
+
+- `MSG` reaches only the clients in the **sender's room**. The `CHAT` gets an extra
+  field: `{"type":"CHAT","from":"ana","text":"hi","private":false,"room":"games"}`.
+- `LIST` lists the clients in **your room**; the `USERS` reply gets an extra field:
+  `{"type":"USERS","nicks":["ana","eva"],"room":"games"}`.
+- When a client moves, the old room receives `EVENT "<nick> left #<old>"` and the
+  new room (the client included) receives `EVENT "<nick> joined #<new>"`.
+
+**Unchanged:** `PRIV` works across rooms. Connection notices `"<nick> joined"` /
+`"<nick> left"` (connecting and disconnecting) still go to everybody, so everyone
+knows who is online. All error codes, limits and discovery are as before.
+
+**Backward compatibility.** A client written for section 1–10 never sends `JOIN`,
+so it stays in the lobby, and it ignores the extra `room` fields. It keeps working
+with everyone else in the lobby without any change. This was the main reason for
+choosing this extension: it adds features without breaking anyone.
